## (b) Binds fixed (F11) — guard_ai.gd:182-183, :237-250, :479-642

- `_build_visuals` (:237-250) now calls `_bind_guard_glb_materials(inst)`
  on the instantiated GLB. Previously the GLB was added with no material
  work at all: untextured imports render white. That was the whole bug.
- New bind chain (:479-642): `_guard_ensure_material_dbs` (same generated DBs
  the `level_loader.gd` PBR path binds, re-read locally so guards never depend
  on loader ordering; exact + case-insensitive keys) -> `_guard_ue_key_for_glb`
  (`res://assets/ue/Content/` -> `/Game/`, strip `.glb`, matching
  mesh_materials.json key shape) -> `_bind_guard_glb_materials` (GLB
  material-name substring first, slot-index fallback — mirrors
  `level_loader._bind_glb_materials`; per-`MeshInstance3D`
  `set_surface_override_material` so the shared import is never mutated).
- `get_guard_material_for_ue` (:535-576): authored PBR bind (albedo / normal /
  ORM channels + `tint`). Every missing-texture path resolves to the retained
  navy uniform `GUARD_NAVY = Color(0.14, 0.19, 0.36)` — the same navy as the
  pre-existing capsule fallback (:258) — never white.
- Fallback behavior (grep-verified, each logs the UE path via `push_warning`):
  - missing/empty material entry -> `_guard_navy_fallback(ue_mat_path)` (:524).
  - entry present but no recoverable albedo (or authored white with no
    texture) -> navy + `ue_mat_path` (:557-561).
  - empty mesh_materials slot (Preview slots 0-2) -> navy + `ue_key slot N`
    (:640); surface with no slot -> navy + `ue_key surface N` (:636).
  - no mesh_materials slots at all -> logged, import material kept (:612).
  - GLB itself missing -> logged navy capsule fallback (:250).
  - `Color(1,1,1,1)` in this file is a comparison only (:557); no albedo is
    ever assigned white. `Color(1.0, ...)` hits are the pre-existing
    alert-indicator / lantern colors, not materials.
- Civilian compare: `civilian_npc.gd` holds rest pose + position bob when clips
  are missing (never white, never errors). The brief's `:152/:208` line pins
  have drifted (current file is 233 lines; those lines are `_idle_ttl` /
  `_has_anims` bookkeeping), but the retained behavior is as described, and
  the guard side now matches it: navy + procedural bob fallback, always logged.

## (c) Transitions repaired (F12)

- `guard_ai.gd _update_guard_anim` (:404-433): the hand-rolled per-state match
  (which duplicated `clip_for_state` and pinned SEARCH to the stationary
  search clip even while the guard fans out) is replaced by a single source:
  `Alertness -> _anim_state_name()` (:389-401) ->
  `GuardAnimationLibrary.clip_for_state(state, weapon, moving)`. Empty role
  falls through to `_update_procedural_anim`. KO / slip / attack-lock
  ownership is unchanged.
- `animation_library.gd clip_for_state` (:276-293): SEARCH while moving now
  plays `suspicious_walk` (ST_Guard search states 9-17 fan out via Move to
  nearby location / EQS; the search clip is stationary, so sliding it under
  scripted velocity is wrong motion), idle SEARCH keeps the `search` role.
- Per-role UE citations added at the call sites:
  `:335-340` attack (Light_A montage both sets; DAM Attack.Ranged is the
  ranged tag, not this melee swing), `:352-355` slip montage,
  `:370-372` slip->knockdown / attack-lock handoff,
  `:323` role playback, `:286-291` setup sources,
  `:271-283` weapon-set mapping. Retained approximation (not silence):
  ClubLantern/Security bodies reuse CLUB_CLIPS — `AnimSet_Guard_ClubLantern`
  authors its own Lantern rows and the Security SK has no Security anims —
  until a lantern/security clip table is authored.
- DAM vs AnimSet search reconciliation (comment, :266-270): DAM Guard.Search
  points at `AN_GuardEnforcer_MindfulSuspicious_Search_Montage_Shortened`
  (stationary tag montage); the port loops the AnimSet VigilantSuspicious
  search row for the SEARCH state. Both names verified in the manifest.
- `clip_for_role` (:256-257): documented as the UE-role lookup; returns ""
  when the role did not retarget so callers keep their fallback.
- `setup` (:187-197): logic unchanged; weapon mapping documented against
  `AnimSet_Guard_Club` / `_ClubLantern` / `_Hauntsable` + both DAMs.

